    <recordUpdates>
        <description>Explanation of validation bypass:
Say an active service indicator is created on March 1 with an end date of March 31. On March 31, the scheduled path runs and unchecks the Active box. However, the flow still identifies TODAY() as March 1, so it triggers the validation rule Inactive_Must_Have_Past_End_Date.
To fix this, a condition was added to the validation rule: NOT(BLANKVALUE(NU_ADV_Validation_Bypass__c, $System.OriginDateTime) &gt; NOW() - 0.00005787037). Validation Bypass is a date/time field with a default value of $System.OriginDateTime. This condition says the validation rule should only be triggered if the value of Validation Bypass does not fall within the last 5 seconds. (If for some reason Validation Bypass is null, the formula substitutes $System.OriginDateTime.)
The flow resets Validation Bypass to the current time immediately before attempting to uncheck the Active box. Because Validation Bypass is greater than &quot;now minus 5 seconds,&quot; the validation rule is not triggered.</description>
        <name>Make_Inactive</name>
        <label>Make Inactive</label>
        <locationX>336</locationX>
        <locationY>384</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Constituent</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>NU_ADV_Validation_Bypass__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Flow.CurrentDateTime</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>ucinn_ascendv2__Is_Active__c</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputReference>$Record</inputReference>
    </recordUpdates>
